meta {
  type: collection
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  Exercises the three applications and two SSO domains described in ../../README.md.

  Every request states which identity it presents and which SSO domain issued it. Auth is left at
  "none" here on purpose: different requests authenticate against different SSO domains, and putting
  a single auth block at the collection level would hide the very distinction this lab is about.

  Before running anything, start both Keycloak instances and Applications B and C:

    .\keycloak\domain-a\start-keycloak-a.ps1
    .\keycloak\domain-c\start-keycloak-c.ps1
    .\scripts\run-app.ps1 b
    .\scripts\run-app.ps1 c

  Application A is not needed - no request here targets it. Its role in the lab (the scheduled
  machine-to-machine jobs and the token-relay page) is observed in its own log and UI instead.

  Full guide: ../../bruno.md
}
